From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mingyang Li <594058+tslmy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:07:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: leave the USB PCS alone in DP-only
 mode

In DP-only mode (DisplayPort pin assignments C and E) all four lanes
belong to the DisplayPort PHY, and qmp_combo_com_init() keeps the USB3
PCS in reset. The USB controller can still exit and re-init its PHY in
this state. dwc3 does that across every system suspend without wakeup.
qmp_combo_usb_init() then programs the USB serdes, lane and PCS tables
and times out waiting for PHYSTATUS, so dwc3_qcom_pm_resume() fails
with -110 and USB stays dead.

qmp_combo_usb_exit() has a second problem in this state. When the mux
entered DP-only mode, qmp_combo_typec_mux_set() already powered the
USB PCS off and dropped usb_init_count to 0, so the exit wraps the
counter to UINT_MAX.

In DP-only mode, only take and drop the common reference, and don't
count the USB user. That matches what qmp_combo_typec_mux_set() does
on 7.2: it decrements usb_init_count when it enters DP-only mode, and
powers the USB PCS up and counts it when it leaves.

This is a 7.2 variant of Joonhoe Kim's "phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Leave the
USB PCS alone in DP-only mode" (v3). That patch targets phy-next, where
the mux keeps counting the USB user in DP-only mode. As its changelog
notes, kernels without 89563a152973 need a variant that doesn't count
it.

On the AYN Thor (SM8550), a 4-lane DP sink (XREAL One Pro glasses, or a
USB-C hub with a display) attached at suspend, or unplugged while the
mux switch away from DP-only was deferred, makes the next resume fail
with "phy initialization timed-out".

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261103135051.1668-1-26rote@gmail.com/
Fixes: 896277138c13 ("phy: qcom: qmp-combo: register a typec mux to change the QMPPHY_MODE")
Signed-off-by: Mingyang Li <594058+tslmy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 5b278fd..5600d22 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -3919,6 +3919,15 @@ static int qmp_combo_usb_init(struct phy *phy)
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_unlock;
 
+	/*
+	 * In DP-only mode the USB PCS is held in reset and its PHYSTATUS
+	 * never clears. Only take the common reference, and don't count the
+	 * USB user: qmp_combo_typec_mux_set() powers the USB PCS up and
+	 * counts it when the port leaves DP-only mode.
+	 */
+	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY)
+		goto out_unlock;
+
 	ret = qmp_combo_usb_power_on(phy);
 	if (ret) {
 		qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, false);
@@ -3938,6 +3947,12 @@ static int qmp_combo_usb_exit(struct phy *phy)
 	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&qmp->phy_mutex);
+	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY) {
+		/* The USB PCS is not in use and the USB user is not counted */
+		ret = qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, false);
+		goto out_unlock;
+	}
+
 	ret = qmp_combo_usb_power_off(phy);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_unlock;
